        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: '27-28 dominoes',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "27-28 dominoes refers to block or draw domino games using a standard double-6 set of 28 tiles (0-0 through 6-6). Players draw 7 tiles each (4 players); highest double leads. Players match a number on an open end; doubles are placed crosswise. Cannot play: draw from boneyard or pass. First to empty hand wins and scores sum of opponents' pips; or lowest hand wins if blocked.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Domino tiles were first recorded in Song-dynasty China, but modern double-6 domino sets and the 27–28 tile block/draw family emerged in 18th-century France and spread through Europe and North America.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Two or more players.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '28 tiles (double-6)',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Domino set, table',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Draw 7 each (4 players); remainder is boneyard.',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
